# Landing Project Registry

## Single source of truth

- **`src/data/projects.ts`** — `PROJECTS` array drives the grid and Hero live count.
- Do **not** edit `ProjectsGrid.tsx` or `Hero.tsx` when adding a card (counts are dynamic).

## Adding a live project

1. Insert new entry **before** the `future` coming-soon placeholder.
2. Required fields: `id`, `title`, `description`, `icon`, `accent`, `tags`, `url`, `status: 'live'`.
3. `repoUrl` must be `https://github.com/reversesingularity/{slug}`.
4. `id` must be unique; use kebab-case or short slug (e.g. `falcon9`, `exoplanet`).
5. `accent`: one of `cyan | orange | green | amber | purple` — pick an unused color when possible.
6. Subdomain URL: `https://{slug}.reversesingularity.com`.

## GitHub sync

Update `scripts/sync-github-repos.mjs`:

- `LIVE_URLS['repo-slug']` — when GitHub homepage is missing
- `LANDING_REPO_MAP[projectId]` — maps card id → repo slug

Then run `node scripts/sync-github-repos.mjs`.

## Validation before deploy

```bash
npm run validate:projects
npm run build
vercel --prod --yes
```

